[0.000848, "o", "W2_BEGIN\r\n"]
[0.965, "o", "\u001b[0m\r\n> build · claude-haiku-5-5\r\n\u001b[0m"]
[0.965056, "o", "\r\n"]
[2.153657, "o", "\u001b[0m← \u001b[0mWrite calc/__init__.py\r\nWrote file successfully.\r\n\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[2.483641, "o", "\u001b[0m← \u001b[0mWrite tests/test_calc.py\r\nWrote file successfully."]
[2.483698, "o", "\r\n\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[3.423424, "o", "Now the edit: add the third argument with a default of 0, and cover it in the tests.\r\n\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[3.762153, "o", "\u001b[0m← \u001b[0mEdit calc/__init__.py\r\nIndex: /work/calc/__init__.py\r\n===================================================================\r\n--- /work/calc/__init__.py\r\n+++ /work/calc/__init__.py\r\n@@ -1,2 +1,2 @@\r\n-def add(a, b):\r\n-    return a + b\r\n+def add(a, b, c=0):\r\n+    return a + b + c\r\n\r\n\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[4.369635, "o", "\u001b[0m← \u001b[0mEdit tests/test_calc.py\r\nIndex: /work/tests/test_calc.py\r\n===================================================================\r\n--- /work/tests/test_calc.py\r\n+++ /work/tests/test_calc.py\r\n@@ -6,4 +6,12 @@\r\n \r\n \r\n def test_add_negative_numbers():\r\n     assert add(-4, -6) == -10\r\n+\r\n+\r\n+def test_add_with_third_argument():\r\n+    assert add(1, 2, 3) == 6\r\n+\r\n+\r\n+def test_add_third_argument_defaults_to_zero():\r\n+    assert add(2, 3) == add(2, 3, 0) == 5\r\n\r\n\u001b[0m"]
[4.369693, "o", "\r\n"]
[5.773753, "o", "Both edits are in. I'll run the tests to confirm.\r\n\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[6.078522, "o", "\u001b[0m$ \u001b[0mcd /work && python -m pytest -q tests/test_calc.py 2>&1 | tail -n 15\r\n/bin/bash: line 1: python: command not found\r\n\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[7.519333, "o", "\u001b[0m$ \u001b[0mpython3 -m pytest -q tests/test_calc.py 2>&1 | tail -n 15\r\n....                                                                     [100%]\r\n4 passed in 0.01s\r\n\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[9.130666, "o", "I created the files and then changed `add`, and all 4 tests pass.\r\n\r\n- **`calc/__init__.py`**: `add(a, b, c=0)` returns `a + b + c`. The third argument was added with the edit tool.\r\n- **`tests/test_calc.py`**: four tests:\r\n  - `test_add_positive_numbers` and `test_add_negative_numbers`, the two original tests.\r\n  - `test_add_with_third_argument`, which checks `add(1, 2, 3) == 6`.\r\n  - `test_add_third_argument_defaults_to_zero`, which checks that `add(2, 3)` equals `add(2, 3, 0)` and both equal 5.\r\n\r\nThe `python` command isn't available in this environment, so I ran the tests with `python3 -m pytest`.\r\n\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[9.167385, "o", "W2_ITEM_EXIT=0\r\n"]
